<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">West Sumatra</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a> is a province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a> on the western coast of Sumatra, with its capital at Padang. It is the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the Minangkabau, a matrilineal Muslim people, and earlier held the centres of the Malayu kingdom of Dharmasraya and the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adityawarman">Adityawarman</a>. In the 19th century it was the scene of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padri-war">Padri War</a> between religious reformers, traditional leaders and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/west-sumatra.jpg" alt="West Sumatra" width="320" height="147" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TUBS · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:West_Sumatra_in_Indonesia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
